# Q26: add uv-plane result entries to /output/report.json. Idempotent.
import json
R=json.load(open('/output/report.json'))
R['results']=[x for x in R['results'] if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q26')]
A=[{"name":"data","value":"Restored raw visibilities (continuum NOT subtracted by the archive; here: continuum from line-free channels per baseline/row, |v-2780|<=350 km/s integrated): Xb55 2 EBs (HCN/HCO+ 2-1), Xb4f 3 EBs (3-2), Xb4d 1 EB (3-2, team-b restore). Dump: scripts/q26_uvdump.py -> out/q26/uv/*.npy + coverage.json; analysis scripts/q26_uvana.py -> out/q26/q26_uvana.json/.log. Coverage in kilo-lambda (bins 0-2,2-4,4-6,6-8,8-10,10-14,14-20,20-30,30-60): Xb55 has baselines from 4 kl, Xb4f from 6 kl (7-m/compact EB), Xb4d only >=10 kl (no baselines 2-10 kl), so Xb4d cannot be matched at u>6 kl."},
 {"name":"method","value":"Visibilities phase-rotated to the N-S midpoint (-0.075,0 arcsec from 156.96346,-43.90461), inverse-variance mean Re(V) per |uv| bin (error = max(formal from off-line scatter, empirical scatter)), ratio HCN/HCO+ per bin; Im part and per-EB spread as checks; plus linear LSQ of N and S point sources (0,+2.55),(-0.15,-2.55) arcsec + one circular Gaussian (FWHM 6/10/15 arcsec, centred on the midpoint) per line. Matched in kilo-lambda, i.e. in angular scale, independent of deconvolution."}]
def res(q,t,v,u,un,c):
    R['results'].append({"quantity":q,"target":t,"value":v,"uncertainty":u,"unit":un,"assumptions":A,"confidence":c,"evidence":"scripts/q26_uvdump.py, q26_uvana.py, build_report_q26.py -> out/q26/q26_uvana.log, q26_uvana.json, uv/coverage.json"})
res("Q26a: the HCN/HCO+ ratio at 8-12 arcsec scales is measurable in the uv plane at matched u (6-20 kl) for BOTH J, and is positive: Re(V) ratio 2-1 (Xb55) = 0.59/0.61/0.60/0.69 and 3-2 (Xb4f+Xb4d) = 0.47/0.61/0.51/0.54 in the 6-8/8-10/10-14/14-20 kl bins; the 3-2 ratio is lower than the 2-1 ratio by R32/R21 = 0.80+-0.05, 0.99+-0.08, 0.84+-0.04, 0.77+-0.05 (statistical), about 0.85 with a ~0.08 systematic, i.e. a modest (~15%) fall that is ~2 sigma once systematics are included, not a large one",
 "N+S+extended (matched uv, 6-20 kl)",
 "Per-bin Re(V) in Jy km/s (HCN, HCO+; 2-1 Xb55): 6-8 kl 50.6+-1.1, 85.4+-1.3; 8-10 42.3+-1.1, 69.0+-1.3; 10-14 32.8+-0.9, 54.6+-1.1; 14-20 21.1+-0.8, 30.4+-0.9; 20-30 kl ~0 (no signal). 3-2 Xb4f: 6-8 48.6+-1.9, 103+-3.7 (R 0.47+-0.03); 8-10 53.5+-2.6, 87.9+-5.4 (0.61+-0.05, only 346 rows); 10-14 35.9+-1.1, 64.5+-2.3 (0.56+-0.03); 14-20 22.2+-0.8, 43.4+-1.7 (0.51+-0.03); 20-30 7.8+-0.8, 11.3+-1.7 (0.69+-0.13). Xb4d (10-30 kl only): 0.49+-0.02, 0.56+-0.02, 0.51+-0.06. Xb4f and Xb4d disagree at 10-14 kl (0.556 vs 0.485), giving a systematic of ~0.04 on R32; per-EB scatter of Re(V) in Xb4f 0.4-4 Jy km/s (several x the formal error) shows the formal errors are underestimates, Im parts are 1-5 Jy km/s (<10% of Re except in a few bins: N/S not symmetric about the midpoint as expected). Parametric fit (N+S points + 10 arcsec Gaussian, u>8 kl): extended-component HCN/HCO+ = 0.54 (2-1, +-0.05 stat) vs 0.57 (3-2 Xb4f; 0.36-0.51 for Xb4d, u>10 kl) -- NO fall in the extended component (spread across fit variants 0.45-0.57 for 3-2, 0.50-0.54 for 2-1; fit chi2_r 2-10 so the 2-point+Gaussian model is incomplete (clumps) and the ratios are indicative); N core ratio 3-2 0.39-0.43 vs 2-1 0.54 and S core 0.70-0.76 vs 0.9 (cores unresolved here; those are Q22 numbers, not new). The comparison is NOT precise at the level of the Q22 2-1 R=0.51-0.58: the 2-1 and 3-2 extended ratios are equal within the systematics, the binned ratios suggest a ~15% decline with large scatter.",
 "R32/R21 = 0.85 +- 0.05 (stat) +- 0.08 (syst: EB-to-EB, Xb4f vs Xb4d, bin choice)","ratio of Re(V) (dimensionless)","low")
